    "description": "<p><i>Reference Book:&nbsp;<a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Star_Wars_Saga_Edition_Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual\" title=\"Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual\">Star Wars Saga Edition Jedi Academy Training Manual</a></i> </p><p><i>See also: <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Construction\" title=\"Lightsaber Construction\">Lightsaber Construction</a></i> </p><p>One of the most popular <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Modifications\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber Modifications\">Lightsaber Modifications</a>, the Pressure Grip is a staple of most <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Jedi\" title=\"Jedi\">Jedi</a> who prefer simple, straightforward <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber_Construction\" title=\"Lightsaber Construction\">Lightsaber Construction</a>. The Pressure Grip senses when the wielder's hand no longer grasps it, deactivating the <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Lightsaber\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Lightsaber\">Lightsaber</a> immediately when it is dropped or <a href=\"https://swse.fandom.com/wiki/Disarmed\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Disarmed\">Disarmed</a>. </p>",
